    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d251">

                <pb facs="0383" n="211" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg211"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111Y2/22a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Spain</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Willard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-27T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 27, 1917, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>291. Reported in press that German Government has stated that <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Yarrowdale</hi> prisoners can not be released owing to
                    breaking out <pb facs="0384" n="212" xml:id="pg212"/> among them of an
                    infectious disease. Ask Spanish Government to instruct Ambassador to ascertain
                    if statement is true and request permission to send representative of Spanish
                    Embassy to make investigation and report actual condition of men. Owing to
                    seemingly unnecessary delay in the release of these men there is a growing
                    feeling of irritation. Hope this matter can be taken up promptly.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
